{"content":[{"c":["PERFUMER*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Also known as an “apothecary” (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.30.25","r":"Exod.30.25","rawR":"Exod.30.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.30.25","value":"Exod.30.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 30:25"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},") or a “confectionary” (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.8.13","r":"1Sam.8.13","rawR":"1Sam.8.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.8.13","value":"1Sam.8.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 8:13"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). This person prepared oils, powders, and mixtures for medicinal use, for perfumes and cosmetics, and for religious use in incense. A wide variety of plants, when crushed, provided oils or powders giving off distinctive odors. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Perfume_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Perfume_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Perfume_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Perfume"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Perfumer","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 30:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.30.25","rawQueryValue":"Exod.30.25","sourceRefExact":"Exod.30.25"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 8:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.8.13","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.8.13","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.8.13"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"61817625c87e0d47c1441489e3e7533a0c91e77ca14b81f0ad9843096d634ed5","sourceItemName":"Perfumer","sourceItemOrder":122,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Perfumer","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Perfumer*","title":"Perfumer*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}